{
  "_comment": [
    "AIC Phase E — THE SHARED CONTRACT FIXTURE.",
    "",
    "A complete, realistic GET /schools/:id/accreditation/twin response. This file is",
    "the CONTRACT between ENGINEER-API (who owns it) and ENGINEER-WEB (who reads it and",
    "never edits it). apps/web keeps its own copy of this SHAPE; this file is the one",
    "that is right.",
    "",
    "It deliberately contains every awkward case the UI has to render honestly:",
    "  • a finding with id: null   — it fires now, the 4AM ledger has not written it yet,",
    "    so ack is DISABLED with 'This will be recorded tonight.'",
    "  • a MUTED finding still in findings[] — hiding it would make an ack look like a fix",
    "  • notEvaluated rows for all three reasons a rule cannot be read, each NAMING its",
    "    blocking signal and the module or intake that would unlock it",
    "  • a standard with risk: null and band: null (no evidence — NOT a risk of zero)",
    "  • a standard with the assurance BYPASS (band 'critical', risk null, drivers present)",
    "  • two domain bands that are null WITH A REASON — grey with a reason, never grey",
    "    with a number",
    "  • a horizon of kind 'none' carrying its reason, beside one 'by_date' whose",
    "    confidence is null (a stated date is a fact, not a projection)",
    "",
    "EVERY numeral in a rationale appears in that finding's evidence[]. That is not a",
    "convention here, it is what the engine's own spec enforces on generated findings."
  ],
